.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Central runtime state of the shell — one instance lives in \fRmain()\fP\&. 

This struct holds all global state, including variables, jobs, history file path, and terminal settings\&. 
.SH "Field Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "t_list* t_shell::aliases"
\fRt_alias*\fP list; alias table\&. 
.SS "char* t_shell::cmd_entrypoint"
-c command string, or NULL\&. 
.SS "t_job* t_shell::current_job"
Most recent job (\fR%+\fP / \fR%%\fP)\&. 
.SS "char** t_shell::env"
Cached NULL-terminated array for execve\&. 
.SS "int t_shell::env_dirty"
1 when \fRenv\fP needs rebuild before next execve\&. 
.SS "int t_shell::exit_confirmed"
Double-exit guard when stopped jobs exist\&. 
.SS "char* t_shell::history_file"
Path from $HISTFILE or $HOME/\&.sh_history\&. 
.SS "int t_shell::interactive"
1 if stdin is a TTY (prompt + readline active)\&. 
.SS "t_list* t_shell::jobs"
\fRt_job*\fP list; all known jobs\&. 
.SS "int t_shell::last_exit_status"
Value of \fR$?\fP\&. 
.SS "struct termios t_shell::original_termios"
Saved terminal attributes, restored on exit\&. 
.SS "int t_shell::running"
Main loop flag; set to 0 to exit\&. 
.SS "pid_t t_shell::shell_pgid"
Shell's own process group id\&. 
.SS "int t_shell::terminal_fd"
File descriptor of the controlling terminal\&. 
.SS "t_list* t_shell::variables"
\fRt_var*\fP list; all shell/env variables\&. 

